# The bare domain goes to the visitor's language. The nf_lang cookie (set by the site's
# language switch) takes priority over the browser's Accept-Language header.
# Everyone else (English, other languages, search engines) gets the English homepage at /
# directly, with no redirect, so Google can verify and crawl the homepage.
/  /bg/  302!  Language=bg
/  /me/  302!  Language=me,cnr,sr,hr,bs
/  /ru/  302!  Language=ru
/  /uz/  302!  Language=uz

# Everything else: pre-rendered pages are served as files; anything else falls back to the app,
# which redirects old links without a language (e.g. /jobseekers) to the visitor's language.
/*  /index.html  200
